  data: {
    LLM: 'After the deal, auction determines trump and point target (40–257). Declarer leads to the first trick. Follow suit or trump; no undertrump unless only trumps in hand. Trick winner leads next. Weis may be declared when playing to the first trick. Score tricks, last trick (5), Weis and Stöck; add bid value to declarers if made, else to opponents.',
    Player: 'After the deal, auction determines trump and point target (40–257). Declarer leads to the first trick. Follow suit or trump; no undertrump unless only trumps in hand. Trick winner leads next. Weis may be declared when playing to the first trick. Score tricks, last trick (5), Weis and Stöck; add bid value to declarers if made, else to opponents.',
    objective: 'Bid a contract (trump or Obenabe/Undenufe plus point target). Make at least that many card points in tricks (plus last trick and optional Weis/Stöck). First team to reach 2000 or more points wins; if the losing team has under 1000 it is a double game.',
    gameplay: 'After the deal, auction determines trump and point target (40–257). Declarer leads to the first trick. Follow suit or trump; no undertrump unless only trumps in hand. Trick winner leads next. Weis may be declared when playing to the first trick. Score tricks, last trick (5), Weis and Stöck; add bid value to declarers if made, else to opponents.',
    keyRules: [
      'Follow suit when possible; may trump on non-trump lead. No undertrump unless hand is all trumps. Trump Under (Puur) and Nine are highest; 157 points in pack plus 5 for last trick; Match (all nine tricks) scores 257.',
      'Weis declared when playing to first trick; highest Weis combination wins for the team. Stöck (K+O of trumps) claimed after both cards seen.',
      'Auction: bid number (40–257) and denomination (suit or Obenabe or Undenufe). Double by opponent ends auction and doubles stakes.',
    ],
