    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 9 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Bid a contract (trump or Obenabe/Undenufe plus point target). Make at least that many card points in tricks (plus last trick and optional Weis/Stöck). First team to reach 2000 or more points wins; if the losing team has under 1000 it is a double game.',
      'Turn-flow example: After the deal, auction determines trump and point target (40–257). Declarer leads to the first trick. Follow suit or trump; no undertrump unless only trumps in hand. Trick winner leads next. Weis may be declared when playing to the first trick. Score tricks, last trick (5), Weis and Stöck; add bid value to declarers if made, else to opponents.',
      'Scoring example: Card points in tricks (157 total), 5 for last trick, 100 for Match (all nine tricks). Weis and Stöck add extra. Bid value (×2 if doubled) added to declarers if contract made, else to opponents. First team to 2000 wins; loser under 1000 = double game. First team to reach 2000 or more points wins. If both reach 2000+ in the same deal, play one more deal to break the tie. If the losing team has less than 1000, the winners win a double game..',
